This code reads moisture levels from three DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0 analog resistive sensors via an MCP3008 ADC over SPI on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the pigpio library. It logs timestamped readings to "soil_data.txt" in append mode, one line per sensor per cycle, with a 60-second sleep interval between cycles. If spiOpen or spiXfer fails, it prints an error message and exits with code 1; if a sensor read produces an invalid ADC value, it prints an error and continues. On SIGINT, it closes SPI, closes the log file, terminates pigpio, and prints a goodbye message, ensuring proper resource cleanup on all exit paths.

