This code initializes the MPR121 sensor, sets up GPIO lines for the LEDs, and polls the sensor every 50 ms to detect proximity on the electrodes. It logs all proximity events to the console with timestamps and handles errors gracefully. The electrode-to-LED-pattern mapping is applied consistently every polling cycle, and a clear message is logged whenever no electrode is currently active. The program also releases all GPIO lines and closes the I2C and log file descriptors on SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

