This code initializes pigpio, opens SPI channel 0 at 500 kHz, mode 0, and initializes GPIO18 as a PWM output. It reads the 32-bit MAX31855 register every second, extracts the signed 14-bit thermocouple temperature at 0.25°C resolution, and checks the fault bit (bit 16) plus fault type bits OC (bit 0), SCG (bit 1), and SCV (bit 2). It drives the fan via hardware PWM on GPIO18 at 1 kHz with a 0-255 duty range using a piecewise curve based on the temperature. It logs each valid reading into a 20-entry circular buffer. On SPI transfer errors or MAX31855 faults, it prints a diagnostic message to stderr and skips the fan update for that cycle. It handles SIGINT gracefully by stopping PWM, closing SPI, printing the full buffer contents, and terminating pigpio before exiting.

