This program reads temperature from an LM75 sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x48 using the libgpiod library. It logs each reading to an in-memory circular buffer with a capacity of 60 samples and computes the running average. The program triggers an LED on GPIO 18 (BCM numbering) if the temperature exceeds 28.0°C, turning it off otherwise. The program uses a background thread with a mutex-protected circular buffer for data acquisition. The program checks every I2C read/write and GPIO init call, handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths by logging to stderr and attempting re-initialization, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths including SIGINT.

