This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and runs an infinite loop that reads the CPU temperature from /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp every 0.5 seconds. Based on the temperature, it sets the RGB values for the LED and prints the current temperature and RGB values to stdout. If there's an error reading the temperature file, it skips the update cycle and prints a diagnostic to stderr. When the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal, it turns off all three channels and calls gpioTerminate() before exiting.

