This code reads two TMAG5110 Hall-Effect Latch sensors connected to BCM GPIO 4 and BCM GPIO 5 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the pigpio library. It logs the state of each sensor every 500 ms to the console. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by setting a volatile `running` flag and exits cleanly when the main loop is terminated. The `gpioInitialise()`, `gpioSetMode()`, `gpioRead()`, and `gpioTerm()` functions are used for initializing, setting modes, reading, and terminating the pigpio library, respectively. The `pthread_create()` and `pthread_join()` functions are used to create and join a sensor reader thread that yields CPU time to the main thread.

