        if (poll_ret < 0) {
            die("Failed to poll GPIO line");
        }

        if (poll_fds[0].revents & POLLIN) {
            handle_interrupt();
        }
    }

    close_i2c_dev();
    close_gpio_line();

    return 0;
}
```

This program initializes the I2C device, checks for the ADXL345 device ID, configures the ADXL345, opens the GPIO line, sets up a poll-based loop to listen for falling edges on the GPIO line, and handles interrupts by reading data from the ADXL345 and logging it to 'freefall_log.csv' if a freefall event is detected. On SIGINT/SIGTERM, it disables the sensor's interrupts, closes the I2C file descriptor, releases the GPIO lines, closes the chip, and closes the log file.

