This code initializes the GPIO pins, generates a random 6-digit security code, and prompts the user to enter the code. If the entered code matches the generated code, it unlocks the corresponding door for 5 seconds and logs the successful entry to 'access_log.txt'. If the code does not match, it prints 'Access denied' and continues prompting for the code. The code handles invalid non-numeric stdin input gracefully by clearing the buffer and re-prompting. It also checks every libgpiod call and file open, printing meaningful errors to stderr and exiting non-zero on initialization failure. The program installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that sets a volatile sig_atomic_t flag so the main loop exits cleanly. On exit, it drives both GPIO outputs LOW (locked), releases all libgpiod resources (lines and chip), and closes any open file handles.

