This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up GPIO4 as an input with a pull-down resistor, and sets up an ISR callback to handle touch events. It also sets up a SIGINT handler to turn off the relay and clean up resources when the program receives a SIGINT signal. The code debounces touches by checking if the touch state has changed and waiting for a minimum of 200ms between touches. When a valid touch is detected, it toggles the relay and logs the state to `relay_log.json`.

