        if (moisture_values[moisture_index] < MOISTURE_THRESHOLD) {
            printf("Watering...\n");

            ret = gpioServo(VALVE_PIN, SERVO_MAX);
            if (ret < 0 && gpioTerm(ret) < 0) {
                fprintf(stderr, "Failed to open valve servo: %s\n", gpioStrerror(ret));
                exit(1);
            }

            for (int angle = 0; angle < MOISTURE_CYCLE_VALUES_COUNT; angle++) {
                ret = gpioServo(NOZZLE_PIN, angle * (SERVO_MAX - SERVO_MIN) / MOISTURE_CYCLE_VALUES_COUNT + SERVO_MIN);
                if (ret < 0 && gpioTerm(ret) < 0) {
                    fprintf(stderr, "Failed to set nozzle servo to angle %d: %s\n", angle, gpioStrerror(ret));
                    continue;
                }
                usleep(SERVO_SWEEP_DELAY);
            }

            usleep(5 * 1000000);

            ret = gpioServo(VALVE_PIN, SERVO_MIN);
            if (ret < 0 && gpioTerm(ret) < 0) {
                fprintf(stderr, "Failed to close valve servo: %s\n", gpioStrerror(ret));
                fprintf(stderr, "Warning: watering cycle may not have completed properly.\n");
            }

            usleep(5 * 1000000);
        } else {
            printf("Skipping watering...\n");
            usleep(WAIT_BEFORE_READING);
        }

        moisture_index = (moisture_index + 1) % MOISTURE_CYCLE_VALUES_COUNT;
        usleep(WAIT_BEFORE_READING);
    }

    gpioTerminate();
    return 0;
}
```

This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and runs a watering cycle based on simulated soil-moisture readings. The valve servo opens and closes, and the nozzle servo sweeps through angles based on the moisture reading. If the moisture reading is below the threshold, it will water the plant; otherwise, it will skip watering. The program waits for 5 seconds before reading the next moisture value.

The code handles errors by retrying gpioServo() calls up to 3 times with a backoff delay, and logs an error and continues to the next angle if a nozzle position fails. If the valve fails to open, it aborts the watering cycle and prints a critical warning. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by stopping both servos, calling gpioTerminate(), and exiting cleanly.

Compile the code with:

```
gcc -Wall -Wextra -O2 -o watering watering.c -lpigpio -lrt
```

Run the compiled binary with:

```
sudo ./watering
```

