This code sets up a simple automated plant watering system that uses libgpiod to control four 5V relay modules on BCM GPIO17, GPIO18, GPIO27, and GPIO22. The program opens gpiochip0, requests all four lines as outputs with active-low semantics, and sets all lines HIGH (inactive) at startup. It simulates an automated plant watering system that activates each relay sequentially for 5 seconds every 86400 seconds (24 hours), starting immediately on launch, and logs each watering cycle's start time in 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' format to watering_log.txt. The main loop runs on a 60-second polling interval. The program checks every libgpiod call and file I/O operation for errors, including the case where the GPIO chip cannot be opened. It also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that releases all GPIO lines, closes the chip, and exits cleanly. Compile with `gcc -o watering watering.c -lgpiod`.

