This code creates a TCP server that listens for commands on port 5000 and controls a servo motor connected to GPIO17 and a PIR sensor connected to GPIO4 using the libgpiod library. The servo motor is driven with a software PWM thread that toggles the line via `gpiod_line_set_value` at 50 Hz with a 1-2 ms pulse width spanning 0-180°. The code logs all activation events, commands, and errors to syslog (LOG_USER facility) and a local file named `security.log` with ISO 8601 timestamps. The code checks every libgpiod call, socket syscall, and file I/O operation, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, releasing all libgpiod resources, closing the socket, and closing the log file.

