This code initializes the pigpio library, sets GPIO17 as an output, and drives it LOW (relay OFF) at startup. It connects to an MQTT broker at localhost:1883 with the specified client ID, clean-session enabled, and a 60-second keepalive. The code logs every connection, subscription, disconnection, and error event to syslog. On a successful connect, it subscribes to the home/lights/control topic at QoS 0. In the message callback, it treats the payload as a NUL-terminated string, sets the relay state accordingly, and logs every received message. If the payload is empty or anything other than ON/OFF, it logs an error via syslog and leaves the relay state unchanged.

If the MQTT broker disconnects unexpectedly or mosquitto_loop returns an error, the client is destroyed, and it reconnects automatically after a 5-second delay. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown: it stops the loop, sets GPIO17 LOW, disconnects and destroys the mosquitto client, calls mosquitto_lib_cleanup(), gpioTerminate(), and closelog(). The code checks every pigpio and mosquitto return code and reports errors via syslog.

