This program uses the pigpio library, not wiringPi, to implement a closed-loop flow control system for an ASCO RedHat 8210 series proportional solenoid valve. It drives the valve via PWM on GPIO 18 (BCM, hardware PWM 0), with enable/direction control on GPIO 23 (BCM), active-high, and counts pulses from a YF-S201 flow sensor on GPIO 24 (BCM) via an interrupt-driven, rising-edge pulse counter. The target flow rate is accepted as a command-line argument `-t`, and the program logs timestamp_ms, flow_rate, and valve_position to `flow_log.csv`. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown and resource release.

